meta {
  name: Stream events for run
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/events/workflows?run_id={{runId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  run_id: {{runId}}
}

headers {
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

docs {
  Same SSE stream as "Stream all events", but filtered server-side to events
  whose `run_id` matches the query param. Events without a run_id (like
  `WorkflowChanged`) are dropped.

  A malformed `run_id` (non-UUID) is silently treated as 'no filter' and yields the full unfiltered stream — not an error.

  Each event is dispatched with a named SSE `event:` line in addition to the JSON `data:` payload. The names are snake_case: `run_started`, `step_started`, `step_output`, `step_completed`, `run_completed`, `run_failed`, `workflow_changed`.

  The server emits a 15-second SSE keep-alive comment (`:keepalive`). When the broadcast channel lags, it emits `: lagged: some workflow events were missed`. There is no server-side reconnect; clients use standard EventSource auto-reconnect.

  Useful pattern: trigger a workflow → grab the `run_id` from the response →
  paste it into the `runId` environment variable → hit Send here.
}
